        "markdown": "**JP NO:** CFPK45EM052A\n**PAGE:** 1 of 6\n**ISSUE DATE:** 7/10/92\n**SUPERSEDES:**     \n**APPLICABLE TO:** Waste Water/Maintenance\n**UPDATE RESPONSIBILITY:** Area Supervisor\n\n## PHILIP MORRIS U.S.A.\n\nlogo: Philip Morris\n\n## JOB PROCEDURE\n\n**SUBJECT:** Lockout Procedure for Secondary Scum Pumps\n\n**REQUIRED PERSONAL PROTECTIVE EQUIPMENT:** Safety Glasses, Leather Gloves\n\n**REQUIRED SPECIAL TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT:** Locks, Tags, Lockout Device, Chain\n\n**APPROVAL:** [signature: M B Aralge]\n**APPROVAL:** [signature: M J Hill]\n**LOSS PREVENTION APPROVAL:**     \n\n**BASIC JOB PROCEDURE** | **KEY POINTS**\n\nTHIS PROCEDURE COVERS THE FOLLOWING EQUIPMENT:\n52-052, 52-053\n\n## I. Potential Hazards\n\nA. Low overhead obstructions and/or congested work area could result in lacerations, concussion, and/or contusions.\n\nB. Lacerations, contusions, and/or abrasions could result due to striking surrounding structures or equipment.\n\nC. Severe crush injury and/or amputation could result from unexpected operation of moving parts of pump.\n\nD. Severe lacerations and/or amputation could result from unexpected operation of moving parts of pump.\n\nE. Burns, skin/eye irritation, and/or temporary respiratory problems could result from contact with substance discharged through pump.\n\nF. Flying objects/debris could result in lacerations, eye injuries, or injuries from embedded objects.\n\nG. Slips and falls could result due to wet and/or uneven working surfaces.\n\nH. Slips and falls could result from improper housekeeping practices.",
